(A `value` holding a list, passed to a list parameter, gives the function a
 copy of the list. The function stores a number in the `value` while it
 runs; its own list is untouched by that.)
a value called box is ["a", "b"].
To 'look at' with a list called items.
    box is 5.
    Print "items: {items's length}".
    append "c" to items.
    Print "items: {items}".

'look at' of box.
Print "box: {box}".
